WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.236
Welcome to MoneyWise SHS, Week Three. In this lesson, practise spotting three

00:00:05.236 --> 00:00:10.473
scam patterns: an account warning that asks for secrets, a claimed wrong

00:00:10.473 --> 00:00:15.709
transfer, and an unexpected prize or rapid-return offer. The messages are fictional.

00:00:15.709 --> 00:00:20.945
You will not make a payment or open an account. A safe

00:00:20.945 --> 00:00:24.000
response starts with pausing before you act.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:28.582
Imagine a message says: Your account is blocked. Send your PIN now.

00:00:28.582 --> 00:00:33.164
The request for your PIN is the warning sign. Keep your PIN

00:00:33.164 --> 00:00:37.745
and verification codes private. Do not reply to prove who you are.

00:00:37.745 --> 00:00:42.327
Contact the provider using an official channel you already trust, rather than

00:00:42.327 --> 00:00:45.000
the number or link in the message.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:49.800
Now imagine a caller says money was sent to you by mistake

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:54.600
and demands an immediate refund. A message alone does not prove a

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:59.400
transfer occurred. Check your transaction history independently. Contact the provider through its

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:04.200
official channel, and let it guide any genuine reversal. Do not send

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:07.000
money because someone threatens or rushes you.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:11.452
A third message offers a prize if you pay a release fee,

00:01:11.452 --> 00:01:15.903
or promises to double your money today. These are warning signs that

00:01:15.903 --> 00:01:20.355
need independent checking. Do not send a small test payment, and do

00:01:20.355 --> 00:01:24.806
not forward the offer as a recommendation. Ask a trusted adult or

00:01:24.806 --> 00:01:29.258
the facilitator for help. Attractive wording does not establish that an offer

00:01:29.258 --> 00:01:30.000
is genuine.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:35.400
Remember three steps: stop, check, and ask for help. Stop before sharing

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:40.800
money or secrets. Check independently through a known official channel. Report concerns

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:46.200
using that channel, with help from a trusted adult when needed. Next,

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:51.600
try the five practice messages. Explain the warning sign and the action

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:57.000
you would take. Then complete the forum, group savings plan and quiz.
